==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈrjɛhtʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛhtʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|réttr|lang=non}} (1), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*rehtaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₃reǵtós}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|réttari|réttastur}}

# [[straight]]
# {{context|mathematics|lang=is}} [[right]] (of an angle)
# [[right]], [[correct]]
# exactly [[full]] or [[complete]]
# morally right, [[just]] (of a thing, not a person)

=====Inflection=====
{{is-decl-adj-1|r|é|tt}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|réttr|lang=non}} (2).

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|réttar|réttir}}

# [[law]]
# [[court of law]]
# [[right]] (legal [or moral] [[entitlement]])
#* ''Article 1'', [[Universal Declaration of Human Rights]] ([http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=ice Icelandic], [http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=eng English])
#*: ''Allir menn eiga '''rétt''' til lífs, frelsis og mannhelgi.''
#*:: Everyone has the '''right''' to life, liberty and security of person.
# [[course]] (dinner course)

